    "db_emissionratebyage": {
      "kind": "static",
      "source": {
        "url_template": "./movesdb/EmissionRateByAge.parquet"
      },
      "extent": {
        "metaparameter": "n_emissionratebyage"
      },
      "metadata": {
        "tags": [
          "rates"
        ],
        "note": "EmissionRateByAge, the national table: 1,590,830 rows, and the SECOND of MOVES's two zero-hour rate tables. It is not an age-resolved copy of `EmissionRate` -- the two are DISJOINT in pollutant-process, and which table a pollutant-process lives in is a property of the pollutant, not a choice. Tire wear, brake wear and running energy are in `EmissionRate` and do not deteriorate; THC, CO and NOx running exhaust are here and do, so a 1980 passenger car is read at age group 2099 and a 2020 one at age group 3. `sbweighted.rs:239-289` reads both and keeps the arm the pollutant-process has a row in, which is why `rtMode_rate` selects rather than sums.",
        "esio_format": "parquet"
      }
    },
    "db_county": {
      "kind": "static",
      "source": {
        "url_template": "./movesdb/County.parquet"
      },
      "extent": {
        "metaparameter": "n_county"
      },
      "metadata": {
        "tags": [
          "scope"
        ],
        "note": "County, the national table: 3,222 rows. Read for one column, `barometricPressure`, which is the ambient pressure the two humidity measures divide by. MOVES reaches it as ZoneMonthHour -> Zone -> County; this chain reaches it as runspeccounty -> County, the same last leg. `GPAFract` is the other column this table will be read for, and is not read yet: every county in this corpus has GPAFract 0, so the fuel-effect blend it selects has no arm to choose between (conventions 30.6).",
        "esio_format": "parquet"
      }
    },
    "db_noxhumidityadjust": {
      "kind": "static",
      "source": {
        "url_template": "./movesdb/noxhumidityadjust.parquet"
      },
      "extent": {
        "metaparameter": "n_noxhumidityadjust"
      },
      "metadata": {
        "tags": [
          "rates"
        ],
        "note": "noxhumidityadjust, the national table: THREE rows, one per fuel type that has a NOx humidity correction at all -- 1 and 5 on CFR 86, 2 on CFR 1065. Fuel type 9 is absent, which is how an electricity rate row takes no correction. The `humidityNOxEq` column is an EQUATION NAME carried as text and is decoded by a `codes` map (conventions 30.4).",
        "esio_format": "parquet"
      }
    },
